OL,3,GNEWSAACOTAR fans put real life on hold
OL,4,Afor latest release
OL,5,
OL,6,FAs I arrive at Waterstones in York
OL,7,Fshortly before 08:00 there is already a
OL,8,Fqueue forming outside the bookshop, as
OL,9,Ffans of Sarah J. Maas's bestselling A
OL,10,FCourt of Thorns and Roses (ACOTAR)
OL,11,Fseries wait eagerly to get their hands
OL,12,Fon the latest instalment.
OL,14,FAmong them is Olivia Bray, 28, who has
OL,15,Fspent more than a decade immersed in
OL,16,Fthe American author's fantasy world.
OL,18,FFor Bray, the appeal goes beyond magic,
OL,19,Fromance and fantastical kingdoms. It is
OL,20,Fthe feminism running through Maas's
OL,21,Fbooks that has kept her coming back.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
